SUMMARY:New Moon Circle for All
DESCRIPTION:Awakening Asheville\nJoin us for a welcoming and inclusive New
  Moon Circle\, where all bodies and all genders are invited to participate
  in this sacred gathering. This event is a beautiful opportunity to pause\
 , reflect\, and align with the energies of the New Moon—a powerful time 
 for setting intentions and manifesting our desires for the month ahead.\n\
 nOur circle will begin with a grounding meditation\, creating a space for 
 relaxation and inner connection. Together\, we will share our personal int
 entions\, holding space for one another in a supportive and non-judgmental
  environment. We will also dive into the astrological influences of the Ne
 w Moon and other energetic currents\, discussed in an accessible way that 
 resonates with both beginners and seasoned practitioners.\n\nBy the end of
  the circle\, you will leave with greater clarity and purpose\, feeling em
 powered to take inspired action as you move forward into the new lunar cyc
 le. Whether you're new to moon rituals or a longtime participant\, this ci
 rcle will offer insight\, connection\, and a sense of renewal.\n\nCome as 
 you are—everyone is welcome. Let’s harness the magic of the New Moon t
 ogether!\n\nBring your friends and remember to carpool!\n\nThis is a free 
 event.\n\n**All donations are welcome to help support the use of the event
  venue.**\n\n**What to Bring:**\n\n* A journal and pen\n* Please bring any
  comfort items you may desire: blankets\, pillows\, bolsters\, eye mask\, 
 etc. We do not yet have enough community items for everyone.\n* An altar i
 tem - this can be a photo\, crystal\, something you found in nature that y
 ou desire to help hold the imprint of our time together.\n* Your sober sel
 f. This is a sober event\, meaning no substances other than your own sacre
 d being.\n* Curiosity and an open mind and heart\n\n**Our Circle Agreement
 s**\n\nThese sacred agreements have been carried forward and adapted from 
 the guidance and inspiration of Jessica Ricchetti and her *[Circle Agreeme
 nts](https://jessicaricchetti.com/circle-agreements)*.\nThese agreements h
 elp us to ground in together whenever we gather.\nThey offer support in al
 lowing us to hold sovereignty in a brave space rooted in love and wholenes
 s.\n\n**All are welcome.** There is no competition or hierarchy here. No o
 ne is more or less than another. We honor the wisdom within each of us.\n\
 n**Become self aware.** If judgment arises\, see it as an opportunity for 
 self-reflection. We are all mirrors for one another.\n\n**Confidentiality 
 and respect.** This is a brave and sacred space. What is shared here\, sta
 ys here.\n\n**Honor your needs.** Move as you need to: get water\, use the
  restroom\, grab a tissue. You are a sovereign being and can care for your
 self as needed. Please try to only get up from circle one at a time to be 
 respectful of our circle.\n\n**Ask for support.** While we are holding sov
 ereignty over sympathy\, we will not offer or assume your needs because it
  may stifle your flow (for example\, offering a tissue could subtly commun
 icate to someone to clean up their mess). If you want something\, ask for 
 it. Trust that we can all say yes or no to your request within our own sov
 ereignty.\n\n**Emotions are sacred.** There is no need to hold back\, apol
 ogize\, or adjust your emotions to fit others or please anyone. Your exper
 ience is your own medicine.\n\n**Witness\, don’t fix.** We honor each ot
 her as whole and sacred beings. We hold space for one another without assu
 ming needs\, rushing to console\, or offering input or advice (unless requ
 ested). Simply witnessing is enough. If you catch yourself trying to “fi
 x” someone\, it is an opportunity to look within to see why you feel unc
 omfortable or notice what it is bringing up within you.\n\n**Names and pro
 nouns are honored.** We invite everyone to share their name and pronouns i
 f they wish. We commit to respecting and using the names and pronouns each
  person shares as an expression of care\, presence\, and mutual respect.
